\fs22
\b Multiplayer Weapon Fix Summary\b0\par
\par
\b Project Context\b0\par
UE5.5 first-person / multiplayer FPS demo. This stage focused on weapon pickup, attachment, tracer, and firing logic issues observed in listen-server plus client-window testing.\par
\par
\b 1. Crosshair / Widget Logic\b0\par
Added C++ widget creation flow for Crosshair and aligned it with existing Score / Death / MatchResult / Scoreboard creation logic in AMyFpsCharacter.\par
Added visibility control helper for Crosshair so it can be hidden on death and match end, then shown again after local pawn restart / controller rebind.\par
\par
\b 2. First-Person Weapon Attachment Socket Upgrade\b0\par
Original code attached the weapon to GripPoint. The first-person skeleton changed to WeaponPoint, so attachment logic was updated.\par
Technical route:\par
- Added separate first-person and third-person attachment socket names.\par
- First-person defaults to WeaponPoint.\par
- Third-person was left configurable because full 3P skeletal socket resources were not ready.\par
- If third-person socket is empty, attachment falls back to mesh attachment instead of hard failure.\par
\par
\b 3. Crosshair and HUD Stability\b0\par
Crosshair widget lifecycle was centralized in AMyFpsCharacter.\par
Technical route:\par
- Create widget only for local controller.\par
- Store widget instance for later visibility control.\par
- Hide on death / match finished.\par
- Re-show on PawnClientRestart / OnRep_Controller / input reinitialization.\par
\par
\b 4. Fire / Reload / Equip Montage Pipeline\b0\par
The weapon component was extended to support Fire, Reload, and Equip montages consistently.\par
Technical route:\par
- Added ReloadAnimation and EquipAnimation alongside FireAnimation.\par
- Added busy-state gating using bIsReloading and bIsEquipping.\par
- Added PlayFireCosmetics, PlayReloadCosmetics, and PlayEquipCosmetics as dedicated action entry points.\par
- Added montage stop handling so fire montage does not remain active after a shot.\par
- Added runtime montage debug logs to confirm mesh, anim instance, montage, and playback duration.\par
\par
\b 5. Fire Logic Upgrade: Camera Aim + Muzzle Spawn\b0\par
The original projectile logic used camera rotation with a generic offset. This was upgraded to a standard FPS aiming route.\par
Technical route:\par
- Trace from camera center forward.\par
- If trace hits, use impact point as AimPoint.\par
- If no hit, use a far point in front of camera.\par
- Spawn projectile / hitscan effect from muzzle location.\par
- Aim from muzzle toward AimPoint.\par
\par
\b 6. MuzzlePoint Integration\b0\par
Weapon blueprints added an ArrowComponent named MuzzlePoint and tagged it with muzzle.\par
Technical route:\par
- Added MuzzleComponentTag = muzzle.\par
- Added GetMuzzleTransform().\par
- Search order:\par
  1) SceneComponent with tag muzzle.\par
  2) SceneComponent named MuzzlePoint.\par
  3) Fallback to legacy MuzzleOffset.\par
- Added debug logs to verify component name, tag, location, and rotation at runtime.\par
\par
\b 7. Hitscan Rifle Path + Projectile Fallback Path\b0\par
For a normal automatic rifle, damage routing was changed to hitscan, while preserving projectile support for future rocket / grenade weapons.\par
Technical route:\par
- Added EWeaponFireMode with Hitscan and Projectile modes.\par
- WeaponDataRow now carries FireMode, HitscanDistance, and TracerEffect.\par
- Fire() now computes AimPoint once, then dispatches to FireHitscan() or FireProjectile().\par
- Hitscan path applies damage directly with line trace.\par
- Projectile path remains available for future explosive / slow projectiles.\par
\par
\b 8. Niagara Tracer Integration\b0\par
Tracer visual was aligned to Niagara user parameters already configured in the asset.\par
Technical route:\par
- Spawn tracer system from muzzle location instead of world origin.\par
- Set Niagara user parameters:\par
  User.MuzzleLocation\par
  User.ImpactLocation\par
- Updated deprecated Niagara parameter API to current FName-based SetVariableVec3.\par
- Added tracer debug logs:\par
  SpawnTracerEffect called\par
  Niagara spawned successfully\par
\par
\b 9. Projectile Self-Interference Fix\b0\par
When projectile mode was active, aim traces could hit earlier projectiles, causing later shots to stop in mid-air.\par
Technical route:\par
- Replaced single trace with multi trace for aim acquisition.\par
- Filtered out owning character, weapon actor, and AMyFpsProjectile from candidate hits.\par
- Set projectile spawn handling to AlwaysSpawn.\par
- Forced spawned projectile collision to ignore the owner character and weapon actor.\par
\par
\b 10. Multiplayer Pickup Prompt and Blue Pickup Light Fix\b0\par
Two issues were addressed:\par
- Pickup prompt could still appear on an already-equipped weapon.\par
- Blue pickup light could remain visible under a picked-up weapon.\par
Technical route:\par
- Made UTP_PickUpComponent::bPickupEnabled replicated with OnRep_PickupEnabled().\par
- Centralized pickup-state refresh to update overlap and prompt visibility consistently on all clients.\par
- Added replicated held-state bIsHeld in UTP_WeaponComponent.\par
- Pickup visual logic now depends on replicated held-state and pickup-enabled state, not only local Character pointer presence.\par
\par
\b 11. Multiplayer Tracer Visibility Fix\b0\par
Originally only the locally firing player could see the tracer beam.\par
Technical route:\par
- Added MulticastSpawnTracer().\par
- Hitscan path now asks the server to multicast tracer spawn to all clients.\par
- Result: tracer visibility is no longer limited to the local firing client.\par
\par
\b 12. Equipped Weapon Collision / Fly-Away Fix\b0\par
After pickup, the weapon and player could enter unstable collision feedback, sometimes launching the player upward.\par
Technical route:\par
- While equipped:\par
  Weapon actor collision disabled.\par
  Weapon primitive components set to NoCollision.\par
  Responses set to Ignore.\par
  Components explicitly ignore movement collision with the holding character.\par
- While dropped:\par
  Actor collision re-enabled.\par
  PhysicsActor profile restored.\par
  Pawn blocking restored.\par
\par
\b Current Status\b0\par
Resolved or materially improved:\par
- Crosshair widget lifecycle and visibility.\par
- First-person attachment socket migration to WeaponPoint.\par
- MuzzlePoint-based spawn transform acquisition.\par
- Rifle hitscan damage route with Niagara tracer integration.\par
- Pickup prompt / pickup blue light replication issues.\par
- Equipped weapon collision causing player launch / blockage.\par
\par
\b Remaining Work Recommended\b0\par
1. Finalize third-person attachment route with a stable 3P socket or dedicated attach scene component.\par
2. Verify remote clients now see correct tracer and weapon attachment positions in all pickup cases.\par
3. If needed, split first-person and third-person weapon representation more explicitly to avoid view-specific attachment conflicts.\par
\par
\b Notes\b0\par
This summary is focused on the technical route used during the debugging / stabilization pass, so later iterations can continue from a documented baseline instead of rediscovering the same failure modes.\par
}
